   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "Rock garden (read me first)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Purely procedural modelling, no model files at all.\n\n① Left column: For-Each (count mode) runs 8 times, each pass takes a low-poly sphere; Point Jitter's and Attribute Noise's rand_seed are both wired to iteration - the same chain produces 8 rocks, each with a different shape. Match Size puts each rock's bottom on y = 0, Connectivity numbers each piece (class). Poly Reduce then makes a low-poly set at 20% of the polygons for the small pebbles (LOD).\n\n② Second column: terrain = grid + terrain fractal noise; a Wrangle colours by slope and computes a \"gentle + noise patches\" boulder weight, promoted to primitives to act as the scatter group (the group field just says @boulder > 0.5).\n\n③ Third column: Scatter and Align scatters the big rocks (Avoid Overlap pushes them apart with Point Relax, Tilt keeps them from all sitting upright), a Wrangle picks a random class for each point, Copy to Points with Piece Attribute = class picks rocks by number - one node places all 8 kinds. Pebbles work the same way, using the low-poly library, no avoidance, more tilt.\n\n④ Rocks grow moss based on how upward-facing they are plus noise, get merged with the terrain, and output a preview image, a 3D viewport and a glb."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
